{
  "schema": 1,
  "goals": [
    "Talk about what you did at the weekend",
    "Form the passé composé with avoir",
    "Use irregular participles (fait, vu, pris, eu, été...)",
    "Negatives and questions in the past: je n'ai pas vu, tu as déjà fini ?",
    "Time words: hier, samedi dernier, il y a deux jours"
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "fr-weekend-1",
      "title": "Hier, j'ai joué au basket",
      "subtitle": "The past: -er verbs",
      "topics": [
        "passe-compose"
      ],
      "words": [
        "time#yesterday",
        "time#weekend",
        "verbs#to forget"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "Passé composé",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "You talk about something that happened and is finished in the *passé composé*. It has two words: *avoir* in the present + the past participle. *J'ai joué* = I played, I have played."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "textCols": [0],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "I played",
                  "j'ai joué"
                ],
                [
                  "you played (tu)",
                  "tu as joué"
                ],
                [
                  "he played, she played",
                  "il / elle a joué"
                ],
                [
                  "we played",
                  "nous avons joué"
                ],
                [
                  "you played (vous)",
                  "vous avez joué"
                ],
                [
                  "they played",
                  "ils / elles ont joué"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "For *-er* verbs you make the participle by changing *-er* to *-é*: *jouer → joué, manger → mangé, regarder → regardé*."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "Hier, j'ai ___ un film.",
                "a": [
                  "regardé"
                ],
                "hint": "regarder"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Two words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "title": "don't leave out avoir",
              "en": "English can say it in one word (*played*), but French always needs both: *j'ai joué*. *Joué* on its own isn't a sentence, and *je joué* is a mistake."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "jouer",
              "tense": "passe-compose"
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Samedi, j'ai joué au basket.",
                  "en": "On Saturday I played basketball."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Nous avons mangé une pizza.",
                  "en": "We ate a pizza."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Tu as écouté la radio ?",
                  "en": "Did you listen to the radio? (tu)"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Ils ont visité Prague.",
                  "en": "They visited Prague."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "Yesterday we played basketball.",
                "a": [
                  "Hier, nous avons joué au basket.",
                  "Hier, on a joué au basket.",
                  "Nous avons joué au basket hier."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
