    {
      "id": "fr-weekend-4",
      "title": "Je n'ai pas dormi",
      "subtitle": "Negatives and questions in the past",
      "topics": [
        "passe-compose",
        "negation"
      ],
      "words": [
        "time#already",
        "time#not yet"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "The negative",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Ne ... pas* only goes around *avoir*; the participle comes after *pas*: *Je n'ai pas dormi.* (I didn't sleep.) The same with *ne ... jamais, ne ... rien*: *Je n'ai rien mangé.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "textCols": [0],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "I didn't sleep.",
                  "Je n'ai pas dormi."
                ],
                [
                  "I didn't eat anything.",
                  "Je n'ai rien mangé."
                ],
                [
                  "I've never seen that.",
                  "Je n'ai jamais vu ça."
                ],
                [
                  "I haven't finished yet.",
                  "Je n'ai pas encore fini."
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "transform",
                "task_en": "Make it negative",
                "fr": "J'ai regardé le match.",
                "a": [
                  "Je n'ai pas regardé le match."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Questions and short words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Questions: *Tu as vu le match ?* or *Est-ce que tu as vu le match ?* What did you do? = *Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ?* The short adverbs *déjà, bien, beaucoup, trop* go between *avoir* and the participle: *J'ai déjà mangé. J'ai bien dormi.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Tu as déjà fini ?",
                  "en": "Have you finished already? (tu)"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je n'ai pas encore mangé.",
                  "en": "I haven't eaten yet."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Qu'est-ce que vous avez fait dimanche ?",
                  "en": "What did you do on Sunday? (vous)"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "On a beaucoup travaillé.",
                  "en": "We worked a lot."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "What did you do at the weekend? (tu)",
                "a": [
                  "Qu'est-ce que tu as fait le week-end dernier ?",
                  "Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ce week-end ?",
                  "Tu as fait quoi ce week-end ?",
                  "Qu'est-ce que tu as fait pendant le week-end ?"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
